thm work this is the algorithm  that determines  which other videos will YouTube suggest  to you as you are watching videos on  YouTube website and this is tailored to  each individual viewer based on their  watch history and other elements which  aren't totally clear to us again because  the algorithm is relatively opaque so  for example when I was logged into my  personal YouTube account this morning  not the show account and I watched a  video from yesterday the algorithm  suggested to me a John Oliver video a  good morning Britain video about Trump a  CNN video from a congressional hearing  CBS news video about 2020 democratic  polling a Bill Maher video from years  ago that infamous radical Islam video  with Sam Harris and Ben Affleck and then  a video from Vice about black  conservatives so an open question is how  many of these recommendations are based  on what YouTube thinks I'm most  interested in how much of it is based on  what is most profitable for YouTube to  promote which may not be the same as  what I'm most interested in and does  YouTube have a sort of blacklist and  whitelist whitelist including channels  that YouTube is going to  disproportionately promote merely  because they've decided that that's what  they're going to do I don't know the  answers to any of those questions but I  have a really interesting data point for  you today and it has to do with my  appearance on Joe Rogan's program last  week viewer Alexander wrote to me take a  look at what he said hey David I just  wanted to share an interesting  experience I've had with your channel  after watching you on Joe Rogan last  night watching today's show my  recommended videos are entirely Joe  Rogan scrolling down I count 10 Joe  Rogan videos all before any content I've  watched recently I've only once viewed  Joe Rogan's content and that was last  night now my queue is full of his  content I know you're always looking for  insights into the YouTube algorithm and  I thought I'd share th